  "headline": "Indonesian Lawmakers Formalize Support For Opinion Rights On Gibran",
  "seoTitle": "Indonesian Lawmakers Formalize Gibran Opinion Rights",
  "metaDescription": "Fifty Indonesian legislators have signed a petition exercising their opinion rights regarding Vice President Gibran Rakabuming Raka.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Fifty members of the Indonesian House of Representatives have signed a proposal to invoke the right to express an opinion regarding the Vice President.",
    "The initiative includes participation from members of various parties, including Golkar, though Gerindra has yet to join the list of signatories.",
    "The State Secretariat stated that the government respects the constitutional rights of DPR members to pursue this parliamentary process."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian House of Representatives (DPR) is currently discussing the potential exercise of the 'Right to Express an Opinion' (Hak Menyatakan Pendapat) concerning Vice President Gibran Rakabuming Raka. This legislative mechanism allows parliament members to formalize their stance on specific state issues. While reports confirm that 50 lawmakers have already signed the proposal, political parties are showing varied levels of involvement, with some Golkar members confirmed as signatories while Gerindra has not yet participated. The State Secretariat, through Mensesneg Prasetyo Hadi, noted that the executive branch respects the constitutional authority of the DPR to pursue such parliamentary procedures. This development has prompted public and media interest regarding the potential outcomes of this motion, including questions about its procedural path and whether it could influence the status of the Vice President within the government structure.",
